  "body": "What & why\n\nBrings the whole codebase onto one DDD **ubiquitous language**, documented in the new `docs/glossary.md` at the repo root. Every concept now has exactly one name, shared by db columns, API JSON, function names, and comments.\n\nKey changes\n\n- **Time:** `tz`/`TZ` → `timezone` everywhere; `anchor` → `due_local`.\n- **One verb per action, db and API alike:** handlers renamed to match the db layer — `add_reminder`→`create_reminder`, `edit_reminder`→`update_reminder`, `remove_reminder`→`delete_reminder`, `ensure_user`→`upsert_user`, `due_pending`→`list_due_reminders`, `add_device`→`upsert_device`, `remove_device`→`delete_device`, `send_all`→`notify_devices`, `public_key_b64`→`vapid_public_key`, `_fire`→`fire_reminder`.\n- **API JSON field:** `tz` → `timezone` (frontend `app.js` + `smoke_test.py` updated).\n- **Docs:** `docs/glossary.md` (terms, conventions, retired-names table, one-line summary); README updated (field names, layout, clone URL now points at the real `reminder` repo).\n\nNo schema migration yet (review feedback)\n\nThere is no persisted database while the app is pre-deploy, so the startup column-rename migration was removed as dead weight. If you have a database created by the old code, just delete the `data/` folder — it is dev-local and gitignored. Migrations become real after the first deploy.\n\nVerified\n\n- `python -m py_compile` clean\n- End-to-end smoke test: 13/13 checks pass on a fresh database (login, CRUD, snooze, scheduler fires one-shot → done, daily advances ~24h)\n\nYour review\n\nGo through `docs/glossary.md` first — it is the contract. Push back on any term you do not like and the code will be adjusted to match. Old names remain only in the glossary's retired-names table.",
